# The committed `shaders/*.spv` are generated from these GLSL sources, and
# `shaders/CHECKSUMS` records the sha256 of the source *bytes* as they exist on
# a Linux checkout. With `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default) a
# Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF, which changes those bytes, and
# `glsl_sources_match_committed_spirv` then reports drift in a file nobody
# edited. Pin them to LF so the checksums mean the same thing everywhere.
shaders/*.vert text eol=lf
shaders/*.frag text eol=lf
shaders/CHECKSUMS text eol=lf

# Generated by scripts/gen-shaders.sh, and binary regardless of platform.
shaders/*.spv binary
